{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa in Cooking School: Indian Food", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Catching Up", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Much, Many, Some, Any", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Much</span> and <span class=\"italic\">many</span> are quantifiers. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are many dishes from India.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you buy any vegetables?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Some dishes don't have much meat in them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There was so much meat!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There isn't any here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">many</span> with count nouns to talk about the number of items.  You use <span class=\"italic\">much</span> with non-count nouns to talk about the amount or quantity of an item.<br>   <br>You can also use <span class=\"italic\">some</span> and <span class=\"italic\">any.</span> The words <span class=\"italic\">some</span> and <span class=\"italic\">any</span> are used for count and non-count nouns.  <span class=\"italic\"><br>Some</span> means <span class=\"strong\">a few</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a little</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Any</span> can mean <span class=\"strong\">none</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a few</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a little</span>.<br>  <br>When you use <span class=\"italic\">any</span> in a question, it means a few. In a negative sentence, it means none.<br> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Future Plans", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>events happening now, or</li> <li>planned events in the near future</li></ul></br>  When you talk about events in the near future, you use time markers and prepositions of time like: <br>  <br> <ul><li>in _____ minutes/hours/days</li> <li>this morning/afternoon/evening</li> <li>tonight</li> <li>tomorrow</li> <li>on Tuesday (a future day or date)</li></ul></br>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Indian", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to India ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love Indian food.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about food, customs and traditions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heritage", "type"